{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T20:23:48.736Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n## What I did\n\n**`src/watcher/build.ts`** — Added `checkStaleBuild(options?)` with a recursive `newestMtimeMs` walker. It returns for `allowStale`, for a missing `src/` (installed package), and when no explicit `packageRoot` is given while running from `tsx` source. Otherwise it compares newest `src/` mtime vs newest `dist/` mtime (`0` when `dist/` absent); if `src/` is newer it prints one stderr line and `process.exit(1)`.\n\n**`src/watcher/loop.ts`** — `StartWatcherOptions` gained `allowStale?` and `dev?`; `startWatcher` calls `checkStaleBuild` before preflight/cycles unless `allowStale` or `dev`.\n\n**`src/cli/index.ts` / `src/cli/watch.ts`** — `--allow-stale` registered on `watch`, typed in `WatchCommandOptions`, forwarded via the existing options spread.\n\n**Tests** — `tests/watcher.test.ts` asserts the new flag; new `tests/watcher-stale-preflight.test.ts` covers stale exit, missing-`dist` checkout, `allowStale` bypass, installed-package bypass, and fresh `dist/`, all via subprocess with mocked layouts.\n\n## Deviation worth noting\n`checkStaleBuild` skips when it's executing from TS source with no explicit `packageRoot`. This is semantically correct (source execution can't be a stale build) and prevents the existing in-process `startWatcher` tests from tripping when `dist/` is absent/gitignored. The real compiled-checkout case and all subprocess tests still enforce it.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/watcher-stale-preflight.test.ts` → 5/5 pass\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit`, `pnpm test` (464 pass), `pnpm lint` → all green\n- Result written to `.run/results/2.md`"}}
